Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a site. Let
$$
\begin{array}{cc}U' \downarrow\longrightarrow & U \downarrow \\ V' \longrightarrow & V\end{array}
$$
be a commutative diagram of $\mathcal{C}$. The
morphisms of Lemma \ref{sites-lemma-relocalize}
produce commutative diagrams
$$
\vcenter{
\begin{array}{cc}\mathcal{C}/U' \underset{j_{U'/V'}}{\downarrow}\underset{j_{U'/U}}{\longrightarrow} & \mathcal{C}/U \overset{j_{U/V}}{\downarrow} \\ \mathcal{C}/V' \overset{j_{V'/V}}{\longrightarrow} & \mathcal{C}/V\end{array}
}
\quad\text{and}\quad
\vcenter{
\begin{array}{cc}\Sh(\mathcal{C}/U') \underset{j_{U'/V'}}{\downarrow}\underset{j_{U'/U}}{\longrightarrow} & \Sh(\mathcal{C}/U) \overset{j_{U/V}}{\downarrow} \\ \Sh(\mathcal{C}/V') \overset{j_{V'/V}}{\longrightarrow} & \Sh(\mathcal{C}/V)\end{array}
}
$$
of continuous and cocontinuous functors and of topoi.
Moreover, if the initial diagram of $\mathcal{C}$ is cartesian,
then we have
$j_{V'/V}^{-1} \circ j_{U/V, *} = j_{U'/V', *} \circ j_{U'/U}^{-1}$.

